    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Office-and-Operations-Coordinator--Professional---Continuing-Studies_JR-1025306": {
      "title": "Office and Operations Coordinator, Professional & Continuing Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: September 9, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the OSSTF (Employee Group) About the   R ol e:     Reporting to the   Manager,   Professional & Continuing Studies Operations , t he   Office   and Operations Coordinator provides superior customer care to all in-person, online and hybrid students, learners,   guests   and key partners .   The   Coordinator   will provide   proactive and efficient reception and clerical support for Professional and Continuing Studies including   the   English as an   Additional Language   program.     The role requires a   high-degree   of organizational skills, process identification and follow-through, prioritization, extensive attention to details, data entry and strong ability to organize, define and execute data entry with excellent accuracy towards student information and financial details .       T he   Office and Operations Coordinator   will:       Screen communications to   determine   the nature and priority of the inquiry, and accurately prioritize and process requests or redirect as necessary;   Assist   students with   accurate   completion of forms, explaining forms and responding to any questions;   Support students with technical inquiries and refer as necessary to ITS;   Prepare, organize, scan, and upload ESL forms and files to electronic files;   Develop,   maintain   and support filing systems in all necessary mediums (i.e., paper and/or online);   Initiate new student and customer records in all necessary systems (i.e., including but not limited to multiple CRMs, Excel, PCS System, LMS, etc.); Update and   maintain   student records throughout the continuous intake cycles for the fall, winter, spring terms as well as special programs throughout the year; Organize all necessary requirements for new and   exiting   staff (i.e.,   submitting   computer access requests, security codes, key transfers, office   logistics   setup, etc.);   Assist   in orienting   new staff   to departmental procedures;   Schedule appointments and meetings for ESL as   required , and register staff for conferences,   workshops   and/or events;   Arrange and attend meetings, book rooms and equipment, order food/beverages, prepare and distribute meeting agendas and materials, take notes, prepare formatted meeting minutes in   a timely   fashion for review/ approval   and circulate minutes to appropriate parties after meetings;   Assist   in coordinating events (i.e., book venues, arrange hospitality and travel accommodations, send invitations, organize guest speakers, all   logistics , etc.);    Support the PCS Operations Manager in all financial reporting duties;   Input tuition/ancillary charges for students, process refunds and follow up with any student payment issues;   Support payment of invoices for PCS and Brock ESL; and   Complete payment processing and   identify   challenges to the PCS Operations Manage r.     Key Skills and Experience:     Post-secondary courses including computer applications, office administration ,   or the equivalent combination of education and experience ;   A minimum of 2   years experience   providing administrative support   preferably in a   post-secondary   environment ;   Strong administrative abilities including ability to keep   accurate   records and schedules;   Familiarity with working in a CRM system   and   in a Continuing Education and ESL environment;   Awareness of relevant University policies ,   procedures   and   privacy legislation ;   Excellent writing,   grammar   and proofreading skills;    Solid computer competency including Microsoft Office Word, Outlook, Excel, web applications, internet search engines, scheduling software, and working knowledge of customized Brock systems such as Workday and Brock DB Contract system ;   Ability to interact with persons from diverse backgrounds;    Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to explain and enforce policies exercising tact, discretion, and confidentiality;   Strong initiative and ability to function as a self-starter;   Excellent attention to detail with a high degree of accuracy;  and Strong organizational skills and the ability to prioritize to meet deadlines .      Preferred or Asset Skill s:   Experience working with international students.     Salary   and Benefit   Information   Job Grade   OSSTF   I , Salary Scale   $ 48,405   - $ 67,147* ;   This position includes full comprehensive benefits including tuition waiver.        This position is included in the Ontario Secondary School Teachers Federation (OSSTF) Union and:    Salary is therefore  determined  by the OSSTF Collective agreement. *    New members shall be placed on the salary grid at the entry level. *    It is Brock University’s policy to give first consideration to qualified internal Brock University OSSTF applicants.    We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
